{"version":"1","id":"devtech","handle":"devtech","name":"Developer Tech","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/57bdcb33c89b43ad8c7af98617b44358","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-1.7428,"y":-3.5569,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":99,"newest_post_at":"2021-10-11T00:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-02-23T17:07:25.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.005051,"listicle_ratio":0.020202,"question_ratio":0.010101,"avg_read_time":2.565657,"summary_length_avg":334.918367,"title_length_avg":69.383838,"title_length_var":170.115294,"tag_entropy":3.237445,"tag_diversity":0.585859,"top_tag_share":0.242424,"avg_upvotes":0.686869,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.060606,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.101449,"zero_engagement_share":0.818182,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":3.01682,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.477612},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-4.6471,5.7647],"cadence_depth":[-0.2206,-6.9853],"hype_variety":[-1.3235,0.5882],"title_style":[-1.8382,5.3088]},"top_tags":[["general-programming",48],["react-native",46],["security",19],["tech-news",14],["google",13],["apple",12],["open-source",11],["github",9]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Linus Torvalds: GitHub creates \u2018absolutely useless garbage\u2019 merges","Developers appear to be losing interest in macOS","Python creator shares his thoughts on Rust, Go, Julia, and TypeScript"],"outlier":["BUILD 2021: WSL now supports GUI apps, Project Reunion and Windows Terminal receive updates, Visual Studio and .NET 6 get new previews"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"z_fi7zeX4","title":"Apple appeals to delay App Store change following Epic\u2019s single court victory","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/oct/11/apple-appeals-to-delay-app-store-change-following-epics-single-court-victory/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/apple-appeals-to-delay-app-store-change-following-epic-s-single-court-victory-z-fi7zex4","summary":"Apple has filed an appeal for a stay on an injunction following the firm\u2019s court battle with Epic Games. The injunction forces Apple to enable developers to direct users to payment methods away from the App Store. Apple has previously argued that its strict rules are to protect consumers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5c4126b788a41c2006d9004f4e1af298","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-10-11T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"9QbDh8qUh","title":"SmartBear releases its 2021 State of Software Quality | API survey","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/oct/05/smartbear-releases-its-2021-state-of-software-quality-api-survey/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/smartbear-releases-its-2021-state-of-software-quality-api-survey-9qbdh8quh","summary":"SmartBear has debuted the 2021 edition of its State of Software Quality | API survey report. This year\u2019s report features responses from over 1,600 global API professionals. The main factors involved when evaluating API tools are ease of use (67%), integrations with existing tools (66%), ease of implementation (61%), re-usability (51%), and cost (50%).","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/516483ed1ff674b31437e32b3766cb71","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-10-05T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"4a7E0Al0I","title":"Linux Foundation: Companies are struggling to find open-source talent","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/sep/21/linux-foundation-companies-struggling-find-open-source-talent/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/linux-foundation-companies-are-struggling-to-find-open-source-talent-4a7e0al0i","summary":"The Linux Foundation and edX have released the 2021 Open Source Jobs report. The report reveals the struggle companies are having in finding talent. 97 percent of hiring managers say recruiting open-source talent is a priority. Two in five companies say they\u2019ve given open- source talent greater salary raises than other employees.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e9c8f96d2a407ed2d068c121d1d2c631","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-09-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"TFT_tVoER","title":"Cardano tops blockchain dev activity for second year, Avalanche witnesses explosive growth","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/sep/17/cardano-blockchain-dev-activity-second-year-avalanche-explosive-growth/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/cardano-tops-blockchain-dev-activity-for-second-year-avalanche-witnesses-explosive-growth-tft-tvoer","summary":"Outlier Ventures has released its blockchain development trends report for Q2 2020/21. Cardano led the way for the second year running with the highest monthly average commits per month. Avalanche, which enables developers to port their existing apps to its faster and lower fee chain, has increased its CPM by 694.4 percent over the past year.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/785c4ad0ff10be0c205bb31c2c2b9cab","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"utfDj3lw7","title":"Travis CI flaw exposed thousands of open-source projects\u2019 secrets","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/sep/16/travis-ci-flaw-exposed-thousands-of-open-source-projects-secrets/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/travis-ci-flaw-exposed-thousands-of-open-source-projects-secrets-utfdj3lw7","summary":"A flaw in Travis CI exposed the secrets of thousands of open-source projects. Travis CI is a hosted continuous integration service used to build and test software projects hosted on GitHub and Bitbucket. An analysis (PDF) from 2019 found that Travis CI was used for more than 932,977 projects.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f74517cd4993273615b154d4bc322841","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"4dn2HJeRN","title":"Sonatype analysis reveals a 73 percent surge in open-source demand","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/sep/15/sonatype-analysis-reveals-73-percent-surge-open-source-demand/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sonatype-analysis-reveals-a-73-percent-surge-in-open-source-demand-4dn2hjern","summary":"Sonatype\u2019s report highlights a 650 percent year-on-year increase in supply chain attacks aimed at upstream public repositories. In 2021, developers are expected to download more than 2.2 trillion open source packages from the top four ecosystems. The most popular open-source projects are also the most vulnerable.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/2bceb668333bad6b7b09ee6624b6b7eb","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"-GCcHlXVj","title":"Grammarly\u2019s new SDK wants to improve your users\u2019 writing skills","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/sep/14/grammarly-new-sdk-wants-improve-users-writing-skills/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/grammarly-s-new-sdk-wants-to-improve-your-users-writing-skills--gcchlxvj","summary":"Grammarly has released a new SDK that aims to improve the writing standard of your app\u2019s users. The SDK provides everything developers need to deliver easy-to-use, real-time writing assistance across four main categories: correctness, clarity, engagement, and delivery.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/29c061f4bb1bd5dea2a6ac76a667d31a","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-09-14T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"uQv1zNxbz","title":"Epic Games scores for developers in Apple court case","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/sep/13/epic-games-scores-for-developers-in-apple-court-case/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/epic-games-scores-for-developers-in-apple-court-case-uqv1znxbz","summary":"Epic Games took Apple to court following the removal of Fortnite from the App Store. Apple justified its decision as being due to Epic Games breaking App Store policy and using its own billing system. Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers ruled that Apple must allow third-party developers to use alternative payment methods.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/51b659c9c3f6729c6092af3c592e8516","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-09-13T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"YuWg1-7tH","title":"GitHub releases analysis of relations between developers and security researchers","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/sep/10/github-analysis-relations-developers-security-researchers/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/github-releases-analysis-of-relations-between-developers-and-security-researchers-yuwg1-7th","summary":"GitHub is expanding its research to more fully understand the relationship between developer and security research communities. The initial analysis, conducted by GitHub Security Lab, has now been released. Many maintainers reported that they don\u2019t find the security research community particularly welcoming. GitHub says it plans to include more insights from the perspectives of security researchers later this year.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ea07a7b3b917722863ee8cfdaa85aac8","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-09-10T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"XjxC4kqRD","title":"Live panel webinar: Bringing innovation to the edge with the alternative cloud","url":"https://developer-tech.com/news/2021/sep/09/linode-webinar/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/live-panel-webinar-bringing-innovation-to-the-edge-with-the-alternative-cloud-xjxc4kqrd","summary":"Learn how alternative cloud providers are helping developers build for the edge faster, easier, and more affordably than ever before. The edge opens a new wave of opportunity for developer innovation. This free live webinar takes place on Wednesday 22 September | 2pm ET.REGISTER FREE HERE.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ce5cda5510c1a6463d58f25727bec3c4","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-09-09T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["alligator","robohub","regehr","alldaydevops","ns"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","horde","on_leuwcq","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"alligator","handle":"alligator","name":"Alligator","is_squad":false,"x":-1.6087,"y":-3.8078,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":300,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/alligator","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":6.719442,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.006667,"hype_score":0.001667,"avg_read_time":3.943333,"tag_diversity":0.193333},"top_tags_preview":[["javascript",73],["react",40],["webdev",34]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-8.9412,-6.6618],"cadence_depth":[5.1176,-4.7941],"hype_variety":[-3.3529,0.5294],"title_style":[0.8382,1.8235]}},{"id":"robohub","handle":"robohub","name":"Robohub","is_squad":false,"x":-1.9741,"y":-3.3449,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":267,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/79911e4f3a514623a70a98793133f536","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.633772,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.005618,"avg_read_time":3.872659,"tag_diversity":0.329588},"top_tags_preview":[["robotics",204],["ai",78],["machine-learning",55]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-7.6029,-6.0441],"cadence_depth":[4.3971,-4.9412],"hype_variety":[-1.0,-2.8676],"title_style":[2.4559,2.0294]}},{"id":"regehr","handle":"regehr","name":"Embedded in Academia","is_squad":false,"x":-1.9615,"y":-3.8785,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":10,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/184fb345011042d887308ece6c5e5f92","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.291355,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":5.3,"tag_diversity":0.5},"top_tags_preview":[["gen